    "secondaryGap": "🔷 single-source-FAMILY — broad + narrow are both wikipron (Wiktionary), correlated not independent. epitran eus-Latn exists but its datafile is absent in this install. The referee records dialectal variants of a word on SEPARATE ROWS (hasi→[as̺i] and hasi→[has̺i] are two independent rows), and this eval scores each row independently (it does NOT merge/OR across a headword — that is the ~1.67-prons-per-word Galician-style merge, which we did NOT apply here). So the 84.8% is a STRICT per-pronunciation number, not a lenient best-of: a dialect-variable letter can only win its matching-variant rows — ⟨h⟩→[h] wins the h-rows and loses the silent-h rows (measured: [h] 84.84% vs drop 84.19%), ⟨j⟩→[x] ≈ [j] (a wash, ~equal row counts). A true best-per-headword reading would score materially higher. The z/s laminal↔apical distinction is western-neutralised AND the BACKBONE strips the apical/laminal diacritics regardless, so it can't be scored either way.",
